Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:06:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] AI_AB_TEST: flags CoalitionCoop and Sanctions (joint wars
 and sanctions against a runaway conqueror)

From the Diplomacy audit's map, two more doors that stayed shut on a
conqueror:
- CoalitionCoop: joint wars could only be asked of friends (Declaration of
  Friendship), and only against targets we were already hostile to. With
  the flag, against a civ whose warmonger threat to us is SEVERE or
  CRITICAL, we may also ask a civ that is visibly against it (has
  denounced it, or lost a city to it), and being wary or afraid of the
  target is no reason not to ask. Not its friends or pact partners. The
  usual desire score still decides (it gates on war sanity, attack
  targets, approach and opinion toward the partner).
- Sanctions: the World Congress AI counted the target's warmonger threat
  only when already hostile to it (approach worse than GUARDED). With the
  flag it counts whatever the approach.

Left out of the bundle until tested (bully test).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj1hm6um5X9SZaXQCRZ
